From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] feat(editor): list numbers follow the list direction, number style
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 2.0 (2026-10-12)  2.0 = merged set of 11 patches (old numbers below)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0002)

(was 0006 v2.0)
- Each list (numbered, bulleted, checklist) is laid out in the direction of
  its own first item with text: the item's explicit direction, or else its
  first strong character (ListDirection extension sets the list's dir).
  Replaces the upstream :has(p:dir(rtl)) rule. Logical margins/padding.
- Numbers: Persian digits in right-to-left lists (every level), Western
  digits in left-to-right ones (nested left-to-right lists keep a. / i.).
- Number style 1. / 1) / 1- (Persian digits in RTL lists): "Number style"
  menu in the formatting toolbar (setListStyle), or typed at the start of a
  line. Defined with @counter-style in index.html. Markdown keeps "1)";
  "1-" is written as "1.".
- Static HTML without the editor falls back to the first paragraph of the
  first item for direction and digits.
- The number takes the font and size of the item's text (::marker rule).
- The html lang attribute follows the user language, also after a change.

